{"name":"Plume","hex":"#a5cfd5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Plume","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Plume"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plume (feather)","blocks":[{"text":"A plume is a special type of bird feather, possessed by egrets, ostriches, birds of paradise, quetzals, pheasants, peacocks and quails. They often have a decorative or ornamental purpose, commonly used among marching bands and the military, worn on the hat or helmet of the wearer. Famously by the blues & royals and the Life Guards. When used on military headdresses, the clipped feather plume is referred to as the hackle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Cavalier_Garde_R%C3%A9publicaine_trois-quart_dos.jpg/330px-Cavalier_Garde_R%C3%A9publicaine_trois-quart_dos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plume_(feather)","wikidata":"Q7205412"},{"title":"Plume (fluid dynamics)","blocks":[{"text":"In hydrodynamics, a plume or a column is a vertical body of one fluid moving through another. Several effects control the motion of the fluid, including momentum (inertia), diffusion, and buoyancy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Defense.gov_photo_essay_100506-N-6070S-346.jpg/330px-Defense.gov_photo_essay_100506-N-6070S-346.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plume_(fluid_dynamics)","wikidata":"Q3817528"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Pulp_mill_steam_plume.jpg/250px-Pulp_mill_steam_plume.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Pulp_mill_steam_plume.jpg/500px-Pulp_mill_steam_plume.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x",